<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  The local-job claimer for West Peek OS (Plan A, 20 Sep 2026).

  WHAT IT IS. Porter's hands on her Mac: claims LOCAL_JOB runs the Worker parks for a card kind
  registered in src/shared/work/localJobs.ts (today: WEB_PROPERTY_CHANGE), runs the duty script for
  that kind in a git worktree of the target repo with the model scripts/claimer/model-roles.json
  names for the phase (Codex hands-on, Claude plans and keeps anything confidential), keeps the Mac awake while it does,
  pings every minute, stops the job at its ceiling, and reports what came back. It never creates
  work, never chooses a model or a phase, and never lands anything without the recorded approval and
  the recorded green check the job carries. See scripts/claimer/local-job-claimer.mjs.

  SEPARATE FROM THE SEAT CLAIMER AND THE MEET LISTENER, on purpose: its own label, its own log, its
  own process, so a hung build can never stall an answer or the room's ears, and `launchctl unload`
  on one never touches the others. It presents the SAME Access service token (the Mac's own).

  NO SECRET IS IN THIS FILE: the two Access token halves and the Drive service account come out of
  the encrypted vault at launch through `vault.mjs run --` and exist only in the child's environment.

  THE MAC'S DAY (owner's ruling 21 Nov 2026, Central): a LIGHT job, claiming only 10:00-21:59 CT. It
  runs behind `~/bin/mac-window run LIGHT` (woken outside the window, the guard prints OUTSIDE_WINDOW,
  leaves one pending record and exits 0), and the claimer asks `mac-window check LIGHT` before every
  claim, so at 22:00 it finishes the job in hand and exits 0. launchd ticks it every 15 minutes
  (StartInterval) and at boot (RunAtLoad): outside the window each tick is one OUTSIDE_WINDOW line,
  inside the first tick after 10:00 CT starts it. No clock hour, so the Mac's zone never moves it.

  KeepAlive restarts it on a NON-ZERO exit only: when the repo's HEAD moved while it was idle
  (`restartIfRepoMoved` exits 75; that is how landed code reaches this long-lived process), when a
  tool or the vault is missing, or with no guard (78). A clean exit 0 is the window closing, so it is
  not restarted overnight. ThrottleInterval so a missing vault or tool is one line every five minutes
  inside the window, not a spin.

  Install or reload ONLY with `npm run launchd:install:local-jobs` (it writes __HOME__ and reloads
  through ~/bin/launchd-reload). Proven by boss-os `npm run mac-day:check` (Schedule row wpos-local-jobs).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>ventures.westpeek.os.local-jobs</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>__HOME__/bin/mac-window</string><string>run</string><string>LIGHT</string><string>ventures.westpeek.os.local-jobs</string><string>--</string>
    <string>/bin/sh</string>
    <string>-lc</string>
    <!-- `exec` so launchd supervises node itself (mac-window execs a LIGHT job in place). -->
    <string>cd "$HOME/GitHub/west-peek-os" &amp;&amp; exec node scripts/vault/vault.mjs run -- node scripts/claimer/local-job-claimer.mjs</string>
  </array>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>
  <!-- A tick every 15 minutes, never a clock hour: the guard reads Central itself, so a Mac on Eastern
       (she travels) still starts at 10:00-10:15 CT. While the claimer runs, launchd starts no second copy. -->
  <key>StartInterval</key>
  <integer>900</integer>
  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <dict>
    <key>SuccessfulExit</key>
    <false/>
  </dict>
  <key>ThrottleInterval</key>
  <integer>300</integer>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>/tmp/westpeek-os-local-jobs.log</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>/tmp/westpeek-os-local-jobs.err.log</string>

  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>

  <!-- Homebrew's bin must be on PATH or `claude` and `gh` are not found; `-lc` loads the login shell too. -->
  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin</string>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
